WEBVTT

1
00:00:04.512 --> 00:00:11.016
A dwikkoji isn't essential, but it's an important accent that brings expression to what might otherwise be a plain-looking updo from behind.

2
00:00:11.352 --> 00:00:20.832
Guests often see the wedding parent from behind or from the side while greeting them, and especially during the candle-lighting walk down the aisle, all eyes are on the back of the head.

3
00:00:21.168 --> 00:00:29.784
A single elegant dwikkoji that matches the hanbok's color can elevate the wedding parent's presence dramatically, so we recommend having one ready if you can.

4
00:00:30.120 --> 00:00:33.576
One dwikkoji is all it takes to give a plain back view real personality.
